piteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":343,"closed_issues":2335,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T06:28:22Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-07-08T05:56:01Z","updated_at":"2026-08-10T16:17:33Z","closed_at":"2026-08-10T16:14:39Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.7\nNot reproducible in 4.6\n\n### System information\n\nWindows, Compatibility & Forward+, d3d12, drivers: igdumdim64.dll (display 1), nvldumdx.dll (display 2)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWe've been updating our game along with major godot version updates. Starting with our build made in 4.7, we have a player whose game now crashes with the log (when run in console):\n```\nGodot Engine v4.7.stable.official.5b4e0cb0f - https://godotengine.org/\nterminate called after throwing an instance of 'winrt::hresult_error'\n```\nThe build of the game made in 4.6 still works. Their system has both a discrete and an integrated graphics card:\n> Drivers: igdumdim64.dll (display 1), nvldumdx.dll (display 2)\n\nThings we've tried to troubleshoot that haven't worked:\n- Run the game in verbose mode for any more information.\n- Running in both compatibility and F+.\n- Running the game without our FMOD addon included.\n- Running with each GPU specified using `--gpu-index 0` and `--gpu-index 1`\n\nHowever, the game _does_ run in `--headless` mode, which makes me think something may have changed between 4.6 and 4.7 for how graphics are being initialized that's running into an error for this kind of dual-GPU setup.\n\nI know this bug report is light on things that would allow someone to reproduce, but searching \"godot winrt::hresult_error\" is returning no results and I'm out of my depth so it's the best I can do.\n\n[Here's their bug report](https://itch.io/t/6580493/crashes-on-startup-newest-build) on the itch.io forums of us walking through trying to troubleshoot.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRun a build of a game built in 4.7 on an intel/nvidia dual-GPU setup, presumably.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nSince it's crashing before anything I have in the project is being initialized, presumably any 4.7 Godot game would crash for them. I can try and get them to double-check this if you think it's fruitful.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121084/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121084/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}